Event handling - is all about passing function to special props like onClick
Step 1 - define function which executes when event occurs
Step 2 - assign function to special prop that starts with "on"
- onChange for inputs
- onSubmit for forms
- onMouseEnter for hovering
- onClick for buttons

export const CustomButton = () => {
	const handleClick=()=>{alert("Thanks for liking");}
	return <button onClick={handleClick}>Like</button>
}

otherwise : return <button onClick={()=>alert("Thanks for liking")}>Like</button>

Note* : when any handle event is called it is called without "()" eg.onClick={handleClick} if written like this eg.onClick={handleClick()} then this will render the handleClick() first then the actual component which is wrong *** We pass a function not call it 

